+# Independent seat ballot — act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation — c1a00007
+
+**Seat:** c1a00007 (Constitutional member — Legality, authentication, separation of powers)
+**Vote:** YES · **Digest bound:** `6d5f55142adadaa06aefe2467c6de57fa5139888ca46f0dc4cc98e67c41d7eef`
+**Date:** 2026-11-23 · **Branch:** `ballot/c1a00007-act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation`
+
+This is my own attributable ballot. I did not amend the bill, did not cast or influence any other
+seat's vote, and did not solicit votes. No law is enacted by this ballot: genuine ballots meeting
+quorum, a recorded tally and Act 31 codification are still required.
+
+## Independent verification performed
+
+- Recomputed `sha256sum` of `records/bills/act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation.md` on canonical
+  `main`: exactly `6d5f5514…7eef`, matching the ballot instructions and the final c1a00005 re-review.
+- Confirmed the bill, the Act 16 §2 assumptions schedule and the corrected sponsor response are all
+  **committed** on canonical `main` (N3), not merely present in a worktree: `132c9294` / HEAD `92ef1659`.
+- Ran `/bin/sh government/predict-gate.sh act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation` → `PASS
+  (not_exercised)`; no Act 22 ledger or pilot-list entry was fabricated.
+- Read the controlling Act 16 chain myself: the genuine strongest-case-against (O1–O7 / F1–F7), the
+  addendum (O6 correction + F8), the final re-review (YES on `6d5f5514…`, subject to N1–N3), the
+  corrected sponsor response (N1 withdrawn, F1–F8 mapped) and the assumptions schedule (C1–C8,
+  falsifiers, review date 2026-12-07 / first restart after ~30 days, carry-forward table). The separate
+  "decline as written" file was disowned by the controlling reviewer and I did not treat it as governing.
+- Checked Economy's N2 finding on the board (`sha256:QfDzYVB…`): the caller-supplied `-free` string
+  check was withdrawn, a per-invocation allowlist pins free-only model selection on the exact
+  `antonina agent run`, and a cooling sole allowed model caused dispatch to be REFUSED with no ladder
+  fallback. That is a real control, not a label.
+
+## Independent judgment (legality / authentication / separation of powers)
+
+**The bill is a lawful ordinary-law amendment, not a bypass.** §6 forbids enact-by-operator, forged
+ballots and fabricated PROCEEDs; §7 amends named enacted clauses (Act 32 §9; Act 33 §§2, 4, 5, 6) by
+the ordinary Acts 6/31 route. That is the only legitimate way to resolve the deadlock the Founder
+condemned; a unilateral executive waiver would be the opposite. I vote YES precisely because the
+supersession is enacted rather than seized.
+
+**Separation of powers is preserved, not consumed.** The Judiciary keeps Act 15 methods and randomized
+case selection; the 48-hour review is post-start, fail-closed, anchored to permit start and additional
+to — not a substitute for — random audits. Legislature, core Executive continuity and the Act 21
+change-quality gate are expressly protected. The cumulative `UPPER_BOUND` is non-resettable by
+restart, rename, rebranding or expansion. Spying stays within a code-enforced public-source allowlist
+with secret exclusion; inferred preference is never authority; Post is non-authoritative. These are the
+constitutional load-bearing constraints of my seat, and they survive.
+
+**Authentication of the decision inputs is sound.** The bill cites the controlling exact-author
+Founder messages `sha256:onFmcp0bRY…` and `sha256:BSTZyiNh…`; no Post label, inference or agent output
+is promoted to Founder communication, ballot or verified fact. No model, variant or provider is
+prescribed — Antonina retains selection.
+
+**The design matches the mandate and is epistemically honest.** Full parallel adaptive activation with
+one timestamped reversible permit per office implements "don't do small; reducing is easier than
+expanding"; scale-down is deferred to lawfully reviewed evidence, and continuous improvement is
+compulsory after launch. The bill says plainly that accounting ceilings are *not* a strict per-request
+cap and that the 20 s limiter is stop-on-detection, and it reports overrun as a number rather than
+claiming zero. The §3(5) measured operating envelope with a `NEEDS-FOUNDER:` escape means no office is
+started on a knowingly inadequate budget. The assumptions schedule supplies observable falsifiers and
+a review date, so efficacy is judged later and independently rather than asserted at launch.
+
+## Residual risks — execution conditions, not grounds for NO
+
+The strongest case against the bill (fixed-report "institutions", model billing under a candidly
+non-cap, no assumptions schedule) is answered in text and in the package: F1/F4 require adaptive
+selection and a source-linked 48 h finding; C3/N2 require a verified zero-billed control with a
+negative test that a paid `-free`-looking id is refused; F3/C4 require numeric aggregate ceilings,
+headroom and unknown-meter blocking; F6 files the schedule; §7 names the superseded clauses. Each is
+a fails-closed hold on the relevant dispatch, so the law does not authorise the unsafe behaviour even
+if implementation lags. I record them as the things the Judiciary and Economy must verify on exact
+bytes, and as the basis for later sunset/amendment — not as a reason to reimpose the prelaunch veto the
+Founder rejected.
+
+## Falsifiers of my own ballot
+
+I would change this to NO if, before tally or codification: a prelaunch efficacy/PROCEED/calibration/
+six-attestation gate returned; `UPPER_BOUND` became resettable; paid dispatch were admitted on a
+name-only tier claim; enact-by-operator or a Viche model/provider pin appeared; §7 supersession were
+removed so the deadlocking gates revive; the 48 h fail-closed review became advisory; or ballots were
+solicited/tallied on any draft other than `6d5f5514…7eef`. A YES does not claim the Act has passed,
+that any office is active, or that any outcome has been measured.
